WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.387
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:10.250
[APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I'm standing at my position, glancing

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.740
around at my teammates around me, my
heart is pounding, my muscles are tense.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.525
I'm ready to sprint, the whistle blows,
and the ball is in the air.

00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:22.070
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; My first international rugby game,

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.150
Luxembourg against Germany has started.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.360
We tackle, we fall, we get back up,
and we all gave our best.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.360
So in the end, we celebrated ourselves
together with the German team.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.500
Why am I telling this story?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.320
Team sports is about a lot more than
just exercising together with others.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.430
Team sports have great benefits for
individuals, for

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.180
companies, and for communities.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.630
So, what's in it for you as an individual?

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:58.430
We all know that regular exercise
has physical and mental benefits.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.028
So I don't need to go into detail for
that, but I just wanted to say it anyways.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:05.370
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But, did you know that,

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.750
three out of four corporate
executives play team sports?

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:14.657
Look at the CEOs of HP,
GE, Bank of America.

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:18.801
I'm not saying to you that team sports
will guarantee you a higher salary and

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.690
a better position.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:25.742
But I can tell you, that there's a great
correlation between leadership qualities,

00:01:25.742 --> 00:01:27.414
and having played on a team.

00:01:29.424 --> 00:01:32.196
As I learned from former Dean Bob Josh,

00:01:32.196 --> 00:01:36.650
great leadership is easy to recognize,
but hard to practice.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.220
Team sports give you a platform to
practice these leadership skills.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:46.840
Where else would you learn how to make
decisions under pressure, inspire others

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.374
around you, learn to deal with failures,
and take over responsibility?

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.424
And most of the time, you're having fun,

00:01:54.424 --> 00:01:56.769
because you're not
noticing you're learning.

00:01:58.279 --> 00:02:02.068
So a team sports help leaders to hone
their leadership capabilities, but

00:02:02.068 --> 00:02:04.890
they also have been benefits for
companies as a whole.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.230
Let's have a look at my job
as management consultant.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.315
I was sitting at the laptop all day,
and all night.

00:02:12.315 --> 00:02:16.260
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Very far away from team sports,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.270
that's what you think.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.430
But then, our annual European soccer and
volleyball tournament came up.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.228
We organized ourselves and
practiced regularly.

00:02:24.228 --> 00:02:27.482
We didn't only get better as
a team on the tournament,

00:02:27.482 --> 00:02:31.886
we formed bonds with each other that
go way beyond this tournament today.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.880
Studies have shown that corporate leagues
instill camaraderie amongst employees.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.001
They improve the work environment and

00:02:41.001 --> 00:02:43.790
ultimately lead to better
company performance.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.690
Active employees require lower health
premium and have less sick days.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.017
Corporate leagues make networking easy,
especially amongst hierarchy levels.

00:02:56.365 --> 00:02:59.408
Make a good position on the softball team,
and then you might be invited for

00:02:59.408 --> 00:03:00.580
the corporate initiative.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:02.939
And I can assure you,

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:06.621
you'll have something to talk about at
the next awkward company networking event.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.507
So, as corporate leagues increase
the bonds between employees,

00:03:13.507 --> 00:03:17.673
city leagues have communities
brought closer together.

00:03:17.673 --> 00:03:22.127
It has been shown that people who move to
new countries will find it a lot easier to

00:03:22.127 --> 00:03:24.870
integrate when they join
the local sports team.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:30.430
Religion, race,
background become irrelevant,

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:36.992
language barriers are overcome, because
the team sport is the common language.

00:03:38.626 --> 00:03:43.105
Many refugees are looking for shelter in
Germany, so do they in my hometown, Essen.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.320
The local soccer team's in Essen,
as does my brother's soccer team as well,

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:54.170
have opened their doors for
refugees to participate in the practice,

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:59.690
so that the refugees can meet the locals,
and both groups benefit.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:04.230
The refugees get to know a new culture,
and they learn a new language.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:10.057
The club members get to experience
multiculturalism without having to buy

00:04:10.057 --> 00:04:12.920
an expensive plane ticket
to go somewhere else.

00:04:15.885 --> 00:04:19.456
But, we don't need to go overseas to
experience how team sports shapes

00:04:19.456 --> 00:04:20.820
a community.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.483
Let me invite you to a trip across
the 101 to the East Palo Alto Razorbacks,

00:04:25.483 --> 00:04:26.721
a local rugby team.

00:04:28.427 --> 00:04:32.988
Former Stanford coach Rob Holder,
has given the young men from

00:04:32.988 --> 00:04:38.710
the former murder capital of the US,
a reason to believe in themselves.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:44.127
He's given them a perspective, and
a motivation to stay out of trouble.

00:04:44.127 --> 00:04:48.326
And he's given them the opportunity to win
the the Division II National Championship.

00:04:48.326 --> 00:04:52.369
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Most impressive is the story of

00:04:52.369 --> 00:04:56.830
Folau Niua, a high school dropout with
already some jail time in his youth.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.150
Being part of that team changed his life,

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:06.610
now he's a permanent player in the USA
sevens rugby national team, the Eagles.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.769
And just last weekend, he played in
Vegas for the big rugby tournament.

00:05:12.428 --> 00:05:16.057
But now, the big question
that I've been asking myself,

00:05:16.057 --> 00:05:18.957
why aren't more people
playing team sports?

00:05:20.836 --> 00:05:24.211
A recent Harvard study has
shown that after college,

00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:28.120
there's a very sharp dropout,
despite all these benefits.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.680
Three out of four adults played
when they were younger, but

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.690
only one out of four still play today.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:40.205
I asked more than 100 of you, and
the statistics are exactly the same.

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:44.889
We here at the DSP are not any
better than the nation's average.

00:05:46.705 --> 00:05:49.765
I'd like to acknowledge that
people find it challenging, and

00:05:49.765 --> 00:05:51.620
myself included to play team sports.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:56.100
You might say, I don't have the time,
you might say,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.450
it's not flexible enough for me.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.473
You might wonder,
am I good enough to join a team?

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:07.941
You might say, I'm worried about my
health, and you might wonder, Hannah,

00:06:07.941 --> 00:06:09.880
where and how can I join a team?

00:06:11.264 --> 00:06:14.275
Think about it, you're putting in so
much money and time for

00:06:14.275 --> 00:06:16.470
your professional leadership education.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.905
What if you could get a good chunk
of it just by joining a team?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.906
So, what can you do as a future leader,
what can you do for

00:06:27.906 --> 00:06:29.643
yourself as an individual?

00:06:29.643 --> 00:06:33.700
What can you do for your company,
what can you do for your community?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.544
I've got three recommendations.

00:06:37.391 --> 00:06:40.400
First, join a recreational league team.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:44.860
It's never too late to get back into
the game or even try something new.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.450
Silicon Valley hasn't stopped here.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:52.300
There's apps for that too, so
there's apps to find other players and

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.500
to organize pickup games.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:59.091
But also traditional methods,
as your local community newspaper,

00:06:59.091 --> 00:07:04.180
a visit at the YMCA, or talking to your
friends through word of mouth would work.

00:07:05.873 --> 00:07:10.130
Second, start a corporate
league team in your company.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.440
This will help connect employees, and

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.970
create a more harmonious work environment,
ultimately leading to better performance.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.230
And, guess what?

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.994
You earn credit very early on.

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:25.790
Third, look for initiatives in your
community that you can support.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:30.360
Like the new grass field for the kids
to play on, to stay out of trouble.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.712
Or, support the local soccer club to
give them new jerseys and equipment.

00:07:41.324 --> 00:07:45.820
Coming back to my international game,
we fought really hard.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.490
We tackled, we fell to the ground,
we got back up, we sprinted,

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.465
we ran up to the others, we gave our best.

00:07:52.465 --> 00:07:58.666
And guess what, in the end,
we lost, and we didn't just lose.

00:07:58.666 --> 00:08:04.146
We got crushed, we got hammered, 100 to 0.

00:08:04.146 --> 00:08:07.456
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But for us,

00:08:07.456 --> 00:08:11.720
it was not about winning,
it was about being part of a team.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.720
It was about persevering to the very end,

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.899
it was about being united for
a common goal.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.210
I believe in the power of team sports
to enrich each individual's life.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:30.206
I believe in the power of team sports to
create high performing organizations.

00:08:30.206 --> 00:08:34.370
I believe in the power of team sports
to make the world a better place.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:38.959
Now, it's your turn to
get back into the game.

00:08:38.959 --> 00:08:42.377
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] [APPLAUSE]

00:08:42.377 --> 00:08:46.549
[MUSIC]

